<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parga is a coastal town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a> opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paxos">Paxos</a>. Held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 1401 as an outpost on the mainland, it passed after 1797 through French, Russian and Ottoman hands and came under British protection in 1814. In 1819 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> ceded it to Ali Pasha of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a>, and most of its inhabitants left for the Ionian Islands rather than live under his rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parga.jpg" alt="Parga" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Γιάννης Χουβαρδάς · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pargapanorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
